jobs.description:
Your new job

For the logistics team of Samsung SDS in Tilburg, we are looking for enthusiastic warehouse and cross-dock employees. In this position, you will ensure that incoming and outgoing goods are processed correctly and on time.

Your responsibilities will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Checking and sorting shipments;
- Processing and moving goods;
- Preparing products for shipment;
- Operating an EPT (electric pallet truck) or other internal transport equipment, depending on your experience and the tasks involved.

You work accurately and, together with your colleagues, ensure a safe, smooth and efficient logistics process.

Your working environment

You will work in the Cross-Dock department of the Samsung SDS warehouse in Tilburg. You will be working in a modern and well-organized logistics environment as part of an international team.

Together, you will ensure that goods arrive correctly, are processed efficiently and reach their next destination on time. Good teamwork, flexibility and accuracy are important in this role.

What do we expect from you?

For this position, we are looking for someone who is motivated and not afraid to roll up their sleeves. In addition:

- You have your own means of transportation to get to work. Due to the shift schedules, public transport is not always suitable;
- You have a good command of the English language, as you will work with colleagues from different countries;
- You are available full-time;
- You have no problem with physical work and are physically fit;
- You have suitable accommodation;
- You are flexible and available to work different shifts.

Are you an enthusiastic Order Picker with EPT experience, or are you eager to learn? We are looking for motivated candidates to join a modern logistics company in Helmond. As an Order Picker with EPT, you will be responsible for collecting, checking, and moving goods throughout the warehouse. Your work ensures that customer orders are processed accurately and shipped on time.

Your responsibilities:

- Picking customer orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Moving goods and pallets using an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Wrapping, labeling, and scanning pallets;
- Performing Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Supporting various warehouse and logistics processes;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the regular day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule applies:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM

- Has experience operating an EPT or is willing to learn;
- Fulltime available;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Performs well under pressure;
- Enjoys working in a team;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Has a proactive and hands-on attitude.

Your responsibilities will include:

- Loading and unloading goods;
- Moving and stacking pallets;
- Processing and handling products within the warehouse;
- Lifting and moving boxes weighing up to 23 kg;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workspace.

You will also perform various Value Added Services (VAS), such as:

- Applying stickers and labels to products;
- Repacking and packaging items;
- Preparing products for shipment;
- Inflating and preparing sports and recreational products for distribution.

You will primarily work in a day shift from 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule will apply:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM
- A 12.5% shift allowance applies during these periods.

You are someone who enjoys physical work and likes to stay active throughout the day.

Additionally, you:

- Are physically fit and enjoy hands-on work;
- Are available to work fulltime and can commit to a fixed work schedule;
- Are flexible and willing to work shifts during peak in July till October;
- Have an EPT certificate or are willing to obtain one;
- Live in Helmond or nearby;
- Have a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Are motivated and reliable.

Do you enjoy hands-on work and staying physically active?

For DHL Supply Chain in Beringe, we are looking for enthusiastic Warehouse Employees Loading & Unloading. In this varied role, you play an important part in the logistics process by ensuring goods are handled safely, efficiently, and on time.

Experience with a forklift or reach truck is a plus, but not required. If you are motivated and willing to learn, we are happy to hear from you. Your attitude and commitment matter more than experience.

What will you do?

As a Warehouse Employee Loading & Unloading, you are responsible for processing incoming and outgoing goods flows. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that trucks are loaded and unloaded on time and that goods are stored in the correct locations within the warehouse.

Your tasks include:

- Loading and unloading trucks, both manually and with logistics equipment;
- Checking incoming and outgoing goods for accuracy and quantity;
- Moving, sorting, and storing goods within the warehouse;
- Maintaining a safe, clean, and organized working environment;
- Collaborating with colleagues to ensure smooth logistics operations;
- Supporting various warehouse activities.

Please note: this role involves physically demanding work.

Working hours

You will work in a 3-shift system:

- 06:00 – 15:00
- 09:00 – 18:00
- 15:00 – 00:00

During your onboarding period, you will typically start in the 09:00 – 18:00 shift.

You are motivated, flexible, and enjoy active work. You are accurate and feel comfortable in a fast-paced logistics environment.

In addition, you have:

- VMBO level education or equivalent working and thinking level;
- Full-time availability;
- Willingness to work in shifts;
- Good command of the English language;
- Basic knowledge of geography is a plus;
- Living within 50 km of Beringe;
- Experience in logistics is an advantage but not required;
- Willingness to learn how to operate a forklift and/or reach truck, or already certified.

As a Forklift and/or Reach Truck Operator, you are responsible for keeping the warehouse and shipping process running efficiently. Your daily tasks include collecting and moving goods, scanning shipments, checking orders for accuracy, loading and unloading trucks, and maintaining a clean and safe working environment. You are also happy to support other departments whenever needed, because teamwork is at the heart of DSV.

You will work full-time (40 hours per week) in a fixed team at the Moerdijk warehouse and are willing to work in a two-shift schedule.

- Valid Forklift and/or Reach Truck certificate;
- At least 1 year of experience operating a forklift or reach truck;
- Full-time availability (40 hours per week) willing to work a fixed two-shift schedule (06:00 - 15:00, 07:00 - 16:00, 08:00 - 17:00, or 15:00 - 00:00);
- Own transportation and willingness to work in Moerdijk;
- You are at least 18 years old and a VMBO or MBO working thinking level (or equivalent);
- You have a good command of the English language;
- Accurate, safety-conscious, and a team player;
